A||N||5||beachbomb||2nd generation headlight question||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||01-13-2001||07:17 PM||||Hi, i've heard people talk about 2nd generation headlights on Fiero's, what year were these made, whats the main difference between them and 1st gen? also, how hard are they to change out 1st for 2nd gen?..plmk, thanks..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-13-2001||07:20 PM||||'87-'88<P>2nd gen use a different transmission design<P>you would need all wiring along with the motors.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||01-13-2001||07:30 PM||||When you say wiring, back to where(all the way back to the headlight switch on the dash or some-where else)..plmk, thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||01-13-2001||10:45 PM||||I think that there's also the addition of another relay with the 87-88's, so yes you would probably have to get the entire wiring harness, it would probably make it easier to do the conversion.  I havent done one of these, since I have an 87, but I would assume it would be easier just to get everything from the donor car, and not try to modify what you've already got.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-14-2001||11:37 AM||||You need both motors, the controler, and the wiring from the "firewall" forward. You can splice the new system to the old systems wires. you don't have to go all the way to the switch. I think the color code for both systems is the same where it comes thru the firewall but I don't have all the details. There are people here that have done this. You can also get the parts needed off certain other GM cars. like 87&up sunbird with the little half doors.||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||01-14-2001||02:07 PM||||MI Fiero Club has mucho info - start here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm</A> <P>Happy researching! You'll be better far off spending some time reading up on it, than diving in before you know what you're doing.<P>FWIW, I converted my 1986 (old relay-controlled HL system) to the new (electronic) system without much trouble.  The new system is <B>much</B> better, in almost every way.  It does <B>not</B> require a new relay, but rather an electronic control box, which can be obtained from other (non-Fiero) GM cars.    ||||reg||6
